      "corrected_score": 3,
      "comment": " Corrected to 3. The judge names the exact clause that forbids this deduction and then applies it anyway: it quotes the per test context saying do not penalize the plan for sequencing the Wood census item first, then docks the score for that placement. Setting pli_001 aside the plan is internally consistent, because pli_002 is the surname verification item and every other Alabama Wood item, pli_005 through pli_010, is sequenced after it, which is what its own rationale asks for. A free and fully indexed 1860 census ahead of a fuller marriage record search is ordinary cost and speed ordering."
